00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:09.000
I’ve always wanted a family. 

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
I’ve always felt that urge, deep inside me. 

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.000
But for this, I knew migration was the only way. 

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The summers in Ghana were harsh, humid, thousands of species were competing for the little food that was left. 

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:35.000
And how could I stand a chance, me, a 14g bird, against the turacos, the pelicans, the parrots. 

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
They were larger, faster, more powerful than us, cleverer against the predators. 

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:54.000
If I wanted a family, if I ever wanted to have something to offer them, then I had to go. 

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Staying was looking at the past. Leaving was about the future. 

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
I had heard so many stories about the great British summers. 

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:12.000
The warm, balmy air, the late sunsets, the evergreen forests with plenty of opportunities to eat and find a mate. 

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:22.000
My friends and I used to fantasise about it, we asked our mothers and aunts to tell us all about their own journeys, how they met our fathers, our uncles. 

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:30.000
It all felt so romantic, something worth flying across two continents for. 

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.000
The power of love. We were young birds, we all wanted it. 

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:45.000
No matter the risks, the cold, the exhaustion, the hunger, we knew nature was calling us. 

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.000
It was a dream, they were sirens too powerful to escape. 

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.000
The greater the dangers, the greater the rewards, we thought. 

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.000
It was fate. It was destiny. 

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:09.000
At last, the day of departure came: there were eighty of us in our flock, eighty young lovers ready to take Europe by storm. 

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.000
We gathered on the branches of a mahogany tree. 

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:19.000
For once, none of us talked. We just watched the sun rise in silence, absorbing the smells, the colours, the sounds of our homeland. 

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:25.000
And then, as one body, we all opened our wings and took over the blue open sky. 
